                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum Prepared by the Staff Committee of the
                        National Advisory Council for the Council</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        NAC–59</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-05">February 5, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In connection with NAC Document No. 58,<anchor
                        n="37" xml:id="d735-f1"/> the Staff Committee recommends consideration of
                    the following alternative lists of probable loan requirements for the
                    Export-Import Bank during calendar 1946. Alternative “A” is presented on the
                    assumption that the Council may consider it inadvisable to recommend any
                    increase of the Export-Import Bank’s lending power.</p>
                <p>Alternative “B”, incorporating recommendations of the State Department, is
                    presented on the assumption that the Council may find it advisable to recommend
                    a $1.5 billion increase in the Export-Import <pb facs="1442" n="1420"
                        xml:id="pg1420"/> Bank’s lending power, which would include provision for a
                    $1 billion loan to the U.S.S.R.</p>
